# THE FILES A COMPUTE ENGINE VM DOWNLOADS ARE PINNED BY sha256: deploy/terraform/ hashes the copy
# in a checkout, and raw.githubusercontent.com serves the blob. A checkout that rewrote their line
# endings (core.autocrlf on Windows) would pin bytes no URL serves, so they are LF everywhere.
dist/collect-linux.sh                   text eol=lf
# Downloaded by Deckard's scan-local.ps1 and pinned by sha256 the same way, and it is the one
# file here a Windows checkout is likely to hold.
dist/collect-windows.ps1                text eol=lf
deploy/report-guest-attributes.sh       text eol=lf
deploy/arthur-ai-discovery.service      text eol=lf
deploy/arthur-ai-discovery.timer        text eol=lf
